ty-50 relative overflow-hidden transform-gpu focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-[var(--focus-ring)] focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-[var(--bg-primary)] bg-gradient-to-r from-[var(--color-primary-orange)] to-[var(--color-orange-hover)] text-white shadow-[0_8px_20px_rgba(0,174,239,0.3),0_4px_10px_rgba(0,174,239,0.2)] hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:shadow-[0_12px_30px_rgba(0,174,239,0.4),0_6px_15px_rgba(0,174,239,0.3)] active:translate-y-0 active:shadow-[0_4px_15px_rgba(0,174,239,0.3)] h-10 px-6 text-base rounded-full w-full" tabindex="0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles mr-2 h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Analyze Page Speed</button></div><div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-50 to-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 md:p-8"><div class="mb-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-5 h-5 text-[#00AEEF]" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path></svg><h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-black">Frequently Asked Questions</h3></div><p class="text-sm md:text-base text-gray-600">Common questions about this tool and how to use it effectively</p></div><div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 md:p-6"><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">1</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Why does page speed matter for SEO and user experience?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Page speed is a direct Google ranking factor and critically impacts user experience. Research shows that 53% of mobile users abandon sites that take longer than 3 seconds to load. Faster pages also improve conversion rates - even a 1-second delay can reduce conversions by 7%. Google prioritizes fast-loading sites in search results because they provide better user experiences.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">2</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What are Core Web Vitals and how do they affect my rankings?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Core Web Vitals are Google's official metrics for measuring page experience: LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) measures loading speed, FID (First Input Delay) measures interactivity, and CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift) measures visual stability. Sites that score well on these metrics receive SEO ranking boosts, while poor scores can significantly hurt your visibility in search results.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">3</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What&#x27;s considered a good page load time in 2026?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>For optimal performance, aim for under 2 seconds on desktop and under 3 seconds on mobile. However, the faster the better - industry leaders often load in under 1 second. Your target should be: LCP under 2.5s, FID under 100ms, and CLS under 0.1. Anything above 4 seconds is considered slow and will negatively impact both SEO and user engagement.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">4</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Why is my mobile speed slower than desktop, and does it matter?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Mobile speeds are typically slower due to weaker network connections, less processing power, and smaller screens requiring different resource loading. This matters immensely - Google uses mobile-first indexing, meaning your mobile performance directly impacts rankings. With over 60% of web traffic coming from mobile devices, optimizing for mobile speed is now more important than desktop performance.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">5</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What are the quickest wins to improve my page speed today?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Start with image optimization (compress and convert to WebP format), enable browser caching with proper cache headers, minify CSS/JavaScript files, and defer non-critical scripts. These four changes alone can reduce load times by 40-60%. Also remove unused CSS/JS, enable compression (Gzip/Brotli), and reduce server response times by upgrading hosting if needed.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">6</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">How does using a CDN improve page speed?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>A CDN (Content Delivery Network) stores copies of your static files on servers worldwide, delivering content from the location nearest to each visitor. This dramatically reduces latency and can cut load times by 50% or more for international visitors. CDNs also reduce server load, improve reliability, and provide built-in DDoS protection while ensuring consistent fast performance globally.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">7</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">How often should I monitor my page speed?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Check your page speed weekly for critical pages (homepage, key landing pages, checkout) and monthly for other pages. Always test after major updates, new features, or design changes. Use this tool alongside Google PageSpeed Insights and real user monitoring (RUM) tools to track performance over time and catch issues before they impact rankings or revenue.</p></div></div></div><div class="mt-6 text-center" ><p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2">Still have questions?</p><a href="/contact" class="text-[#00AEEF] font-semibold hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm md:text-base">Contact our team for help<svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></section><section class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-gray-100"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-